<title>AUSTRALIA: AUSTRALIAN JUNE PRIVATE CREDIT RISES 0.7 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>AUSTRALIAN JUNE PRIVATE CREDIT RISES 0.7 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) said on Thursday private sector credit extended by financial intermediaries rose by 0.7 percent in June, seasonally-adjusted, after rising 1.0 percent in May.</p>
<p>For the year to June, credit rose by 9.9 percent.  </p>
<p>The RBA detailed the change in financial aggregates as follows, seasonally-adjusted in percentage terms -</p>
<p>				    June 97     May 97   Jun 97/Jun 96</p>
<p>    Total credit		 +0.7	  +1.0	  + 9.9</p>
<p>    M3			     +0.4	  +1.3	  +10.4</p>
<p>    Broad money		  +0.5	  +1.1	  +10.7</p>
<p>-- Private Sector Credit</p>
<p>    Housing			+0.8	  +1.1	  +10.8</p>
<p>    Business		     +0.5	  +1.1	   +9.1</p>
<p>    Other Personal use	 +0.8	  +0.7	  +10.1</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
